A||||35||artherd||Just spent more on wheels than I did on the entire car!||||3||
Z||000000||artherd||11-19-2001||12:04 AM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/porsche-wheel1.jpg"> <P>They are BBS (made for OE Porsche) Sport Design.  2-piece wheels, 18x7.5 front, and 18x10" rear.  More numbers:  225/40/18 and 275/35/18.   Should be fun!<P>I paid &lt;gulp&gt; $2750 including tyres and freight.  They are 'new' take-offs (have only 50 test drive miles on them.)  This is $500 more than I paid for the entire car!<P>They are 5x130mm bolt pattern, so I need to do some custom work to build spindles/hubs to carry them.   Brakes are also coming off a 993 biturbo.<P>The Northstar car is comming....<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000001||onfire||11-19-2001||12:13 AM||||WOW! very nice. That's $250 more than what I paid for my Fiero. And $1950 more than I paid for my wheels and tires.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/onfiresigtoo.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Brandon86SE||11-19-2001||12:17 AM||||But, on the bright side, they're gorgeous rims!  They'll help your car stand out even more, Ben.  Whatcha gonna do with the old ones now?<P>Brandon<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Field_Front_(sig)_1.jpg"> ||||reg||14
Z||000003||artherd||11-19-2001||12:28 AM||||Yeah, I wanted some wider rears to take the 300+bhp    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  And I love the 17s so much that I just had to try 18s    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Since I'm going to a 5x130 bolt pattern for the brakes anyway, and wanted quality wheels, the BBS/Porsches were a no-brainer (PERFECT offsets and sizes!)<P>Oh, the Red car will keep it's 17s, these are for my (exactly the same, only silver and sunroof instead of T-tops) Northstar Project Formula!<P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/drop-cradle.jpg">     <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/northstar/northstar1.jpg">     <P>That's the car these wheels (and the Northstar) are going onto!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>(Now I gotta go earn more money, still got the brakes and ECU and a dozen other things to purchase :S)<P><BR>   <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Brandon86SE:<BR><B>But, on the bright side, they're gorgeous rims!  They'll help your car stand out even more, Ben.  Whatcha gonna do with the old ones now?<P>Brandon<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">      <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<P>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 11-19-2001).]<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000004||artherd||11-19-2001||12:43 AM||||More wheel-drool pics...  forgive my show-off-ness :S)<P>These are the actual wheels/tyres themselves.<BR>Note the larger ones...<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/Porsche_wheels1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/Porsche_wheels2.jpg"> <P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000005||Nashco||11-19-2001||01:04 AM||||Wow, looks sweet man!  And very very good quality parts...the investment will be well worth it.  Those wheels are supposed to be very light.  Do you have a scale to weigh a front and rear with, just for curiosity's sake?<P>I won't be in the market for some 18s for a while, since I just bought 17s, but I am definitely doing bigger brakes.  I'd love to keep in touch with you about the brake install.  Have you done much research yet?  Do you plan on installing the brake master cylinder to match it?  Do you have measurements of parts yet?  I could make some CAD drawings for you to take to a machinist when you get to that point.  Like I said, I'm very interested in this, and I'd help you with anything that I could.  I want a huge brake setup on my car, as I think stopping is just as important as going in competition.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000006||Nashco||11-19-2001||01:09 AM||||Oh, a note on the wheels.  I know Porsches used to use a spherical headed lug bolt, rather than chamfered lug nut.  If your wheels have that design, you will have to use the spherical headed lug bolts and shorten them up to work properly with your hub.  Obviously you'll have to machine the hub to accept them.  Are they this style, or do the new Porsches not use that?<P>Porsche/VW has always been cool about lugs.  If you think about it, it's cheaper, lighter, and safer to go with the spherical headed bolt.  What reason is there NOT to use them???  The high performance Porsches of the 80s even went so far as to use aluminum lug bolts to cut down on weight.  GOD I love Porsche! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000007||artherd||11-19-2001||01:24 AM||||They should be light   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  No idea how light yet, but I will weigh them (have a pretty good digital readout scale good to 1oz at 400lbs.)<P>EDIT: Yes, they're the tapered lug-bolt-stud type of wheel.  Matching lug nuts can be found and used with the wheels (Honda lug nuts use the same taper oddly enough) but I am at least going to try to use the (IMO supior) stud design.  BMW does the same thing btw.<P>The brakes I still need to order and recive, but peliminarily all that will be needed are single-piece machined mounting brackets (of course) and rotor-hats. (the rotors are two-piece, so I can 'put' them anywhere I want.)<P>  <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/porsche-s.jpg">  <P>Should be the ultimate in braking for our cars, the 911 933 Twin Turbo 'Big Red' brakes are legendary. "like hitting a brick wall, only harder" that's how they stop   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>They're also going to be expensive.  The priciest single component of this car is going to be the brakes. (just under $4k.)<P>I do plan on using a Porsche master cylinder, and possibly same entire OE ABS system. (if I can find one for less than a dealer would want for all-new parts)<P>Alternatively, I may go for an aftermarket non-power assist master cylinder...  I don't like vacumm assist.<P>We will see!<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<P>  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Nashco:<BR><B><BR>I won't be in the market for some 18s for a while, since I just bought 17s, but I am definitely doing bigger brakes.  I'd love to keep in touch with you about the brake install.  Have you done much research yet?  Do you plan on installing the brake master cylinder to match it?  Do you have measurements of parts yet?  <P>Bryce<BR>88 GT</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>------------------<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">     <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red                     "Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                                        -Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"<p>[This message has been edited by artherd (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||3
Z||000008||Nashco||11-19-2001||02:46 AM||||You SHOULD NOT have shown me those brakes...OMG!!!  I'm putty in the hands of Porsche right now....geez.<P>Yeah, I knew the lug nuts could be had, but that would just not be appropriate for such a bad ass swap!<P>So, you're using all factory supplied parts?  Have you been keeping some detailed info, like part numbers and cost of each part?<P>So, by "preliminary" do you mean after you get the rotors, pads, calipers and before you need the master cylinder?<P>That's great that it has the two piece rotor; not only does it seem as if Porsche was begging people to use them for a swap, but it is also more cost effective for replacement  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>What does your 4k pricetag include?  I could make the adapters and rotor hats for myself very cheap, scary cheap (got a hookup  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">).<P>Like I said, I'd <B>love</B> to see a price breakdown with part numbers.  If you didn't get any of the specifics, I may just have to contact my local dealership  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>So, why don't you like vacuum assist?  You plan on doing a cam that will lower your vaccuum pressure, or you trying to eliminate a line down the car?  Either would be good, but that will be a lot of research to get rid of that master cylinder with equivalent results, I'd imagine.  Time for some brainstorming, eh?<P>Well, keep me updated, I'm hooked now!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT<p>[This message has been edited by Nashco (edited 11-19-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000009||fieroX||11-19-2001||02:53 AM||||I spent more than 3x the amount on my engine and tranny for my swap than I did for my car originally.  $500 vs $1694.  Now im up to $2042 on the swap cost alone.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fierox.com/logo2small.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Elenor84||11-19-2001||03:13 AM||||Thats 1250$ more then I paid for my car...but man they are sweet!!!!!!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000011||artherd||11-19-2001||03:47 AM||||Heh, I know what you mean about putty ;)<P>Yeah, I'll have full info on everything, but I don't want want to speak before I know something :)<P>I've got a contact who owns a pretty good machine shop, (makes radio tellescope dishes for NASA ;)  who will hopefully be doing the milling work.  But I will let you know if it falls through, thanks for the offer! (gotta get metal cut, someday I'll have my own machine tools :)<P>Yeah, the discreet rotor hats are great, give wonderful design freedom, save unsprung weight, etc.<P>Total unsprung weight of the entire setup, from suspension members to tyres, should be just a tad more than stock, not enough to be noticable.  And everything just gets squared :)<P>The trick is to find the parts for less than OE dealer prices (otherwise I'd be above $10k already :)  Heck, the calipers alone (no pads) retail for around $600ea from your dealer...<P>If this all turns out well, I may offer a kit, who knows. (though to be honest, Held Motorsports 13" kit is very good, I decided on adapting Big Reds only because I already wanted the wheels, and based on the idea that if the Held kit was hugely overkill, than the  Porsche being hugely hugely overkill, would be fun ;)  Ok, so there wasn't much logic to it all ;)<P>Best!<BR>Ben.<BR><P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000012||Screwie||11-19-2001||05:36 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by artherd:<BR><B>(Now I gotta go earn more money, still got the brakes and ECU and a dozen other things to purchase :S)<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Hey, aren't we forgetting something here? What about the BMW850CSi?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> Really nice wheels though, I love 'em. I see a German trend there  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <P>I think it's a good thing I don't own a car right now, cause with all the ideas you guys give me, I'd be out of money before you can say "I want a Fiero".  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
