Z||000014||Raydar||11-19-2001||06:58 AM||||Ben,<P>Nice wheels and brakes, man!!!<BR>That car is going to be scary, in terms of acceleration and handling.<P>The old hot rodders saying applies:<P>"There is no substitute for cubic dollars."  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><BR><P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>From the Department of Redundancy Department.</FONT>||||reg||14
Z||000015||Nashco||11-19-2001||10:25 AM||||Wow, I can't believe there are even any aftermarket parts for those.  I have seen some Porsche adapting companies, one company I've seen used <B>TWO</B> of the biturbo calipers per rotor.  They even had a kit for Fieros, 84-87s I believe.  I'll look around tonight and see if I can find my bookmark for it.<P>I don't know how much call there is for a Porsche brake kit there is, I'd imagine Held doesn't even sell too many of their kits at half the price.<P>Like I said, any info you can pass on will great!  Keep us updated with progress, as you always do <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  Heh, you ought to put the wheels in place as good as you can for a photo opportunity!  Yeah, you can't get them on the studs, but you could just stick them up in the wheelwell and give us some more drool material <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
